1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,069
People don't quit the game.

2
00:00:02,069 --> 00:00:03,738
They quit organizing it.

3
00:00:03,738 --> 00:00:06,194
Six messages, and still no game.

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:07,600
This is Serve.

5
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:11,973
Your agent agrees your week with your friends' agents, and you say yes once.

6
00:00:11,973 --> 00:00:15,997
It runs on Muse Glimmer, on my own RTX 3090.

7
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,144
Act one: cold start.

8
00:00:18,144 --> 00:00:21,152
I ask my agent for one more player on Saturday.

9
00:00:21,152 --> 00:00:27,153
Muse Glimmer drafts the invite with the nearest court, and Llama Guard checks it before anyone sees it.

10
00:00:27,153 --> 00:00:30,074
I post it, and share the link to any group chat.

11
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:35,978
Leo has no account.

12
00:00:35,978 --> 00:00:39,324
The link opens the game, one sign-in, and he's in.

13
00:00:39,324 --> 00:00:42,127
The game is full, and I hear: game on.

14
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:50,804
Act two: agents negotiate.

15
00:00:50,804 --> 00:00:52,587
One tap plans my week.

16
00:00:52,587 --> 00:00:56,919
Each friend's agent answers over A2A, with signed Agent Cards.

17
00:00:56,919 --> 00:01:01,371
A small model I fine-tuned answers when it's sure, and Glimmer when it's not.

18
00:01:01,371 --> 00:01:04,831
Everyone agreed, and nothing is booked until I say yes.

19
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:12,885
Or in Messenger: one yes, and it's booked.

20
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:19,648
And it's a real negotiation: Hana's agent counter-offers Saturday.

21
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,289
Act three: courts and clubs.

22
00:01:23,289 --> 00:01:25,372
Real courts from OpenStreetMap.

23
00:01:25,372 --> 00:01:33,544
Prompt Guard screens the reviews first, then Glimmer judges every court, and each reason cites the map, a review or the forecast.

24
00:01:33,544 --> 00:01:37,041
Clubs sit on a real map too, and anyone can start one.

25
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:53,729
Beyond text: your own video, auto-cut into a clip to share with your club.

26
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:55,953
Fifteen Meta models.

27
00:01:55,953 --> 00:01:59,112
Six carry Serve, with Muse Glimmer at the centre.

28
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:01,229
Glimmer needs forty seconds.

29
00:02:01,229 --> 00:02:08,511
The 1B model I fine-tuned on its choices needs under one, and agrees 89.5 percent of the time.

30
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:12,826
Ninety-three attacks, all stopped, under Meta's Agents Rule of Two.

31
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:16,028
It's live, with real players and two real clubs.

32
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:22,565
And it works for school clubs, older adults, a charity cup: any ball sport.

33
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:24,908
Serve.

34
00:02:24,908 --> 00:02:25,893
Play more.

35
00:02:25,893 --> 00:02:27,168
Manage less.

